# Ignore everything, then re-add what the build stage needs. An allowlist is
# safer here than a denylist: the alternative risks copying presets/user/,
# .env files, or evals/results/ into a build context that gets pushed.
*

!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json

!apps/server/**
!apps/web/package.json
!evals/package.json
!packages/helix/**
!packages/tone-tools/**

# Re-exclude things that would otherwise slip in under the rules above.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.log
evals/results
presets/user

# The server bundle ships the curated starter set. Keep the rest of the owned
# and private preset directories out of the image build context.
!presets/
!presets/user/
!presets/user/templates/
!presets/user/templates/**
